      onChainMetrics: "On-chain data would likely show increased exchange inflows (selling pressure), a rise in dormant supply waking up, and potentially a decrease in active addresses as retail investors pull back. Long-term holder (LTH) metrics might show continued accumulation or holding, consistent with the \'diamond hands\' narrative.",
      whaleActivity: "Whale activity could show large transfers to exchanges, indicating potential selling, or conversely, accumulation at lower prices by strategic investors. The appearance of leveraged BTC short positions on Hyperliquid, as noted by Cointelegraph, suggests significant whale or institutional derivatives trading activity contributing to price pressure.",
      institutionalAdoption: "Institutional adoption remains a key driver for Bitcoin. U.S. spot Bitcoin ETFs continue to see demand, albeit potentially muted during market downturns. The \'old money\' perspective from BingX indicates a growing, albeit limited, long-term strategic interest from family offices and high-net-worth individuals.",
