      bearCase: "The increasing regulatory pressure on privacy features, coupled with persistent security vulnerabilities and widespread fraud, could significantly impede crypto adoption. A fragmented and overly restrictive regulatory environment, combined with a lack of trust due to scams and breaches, might deter both retail and institutional investors, leading to slower growth or even contraction in certain segments.",
      neutralCase: "The crypto market will continue to navigate a complex path of innovation alongside regulatory and security challenges. While privacy innovations will face resistance, and security incidents will occur, the industry\'s inherent drive for decentralization and technological advancement will persist. This will result in a gradual but uneven progression towards greater maturity, with periods of rapid growth interspersed with regulatory crackdowns and security-driven corrections.",
      probabilityWeightedOutlook: "A probability-weighted outlook suggests a \'Neutral to Cautiously Bullish\' trajectory. While regulatory and security headwinds are significant (40% probability of hindrance), the industry\'s capacity for innovation and self-correction, alongside increasing institutional interest, provides strong underlying support (60% probability of continued growth). The net effect will likely be a more regulated, secure, and ultimately more credible, albeit slower-growing, ecosystem.",
      potentialCatalysts: ["Development of privacy-enhancing technologies that satisfy regulatory compliance requirements.", "Successful legal precedents set against crypto fraud, improving platform integrity.", "Significant advancements in DeFi security auditing and insurance mechanisms.", "Clear and harmonized global regulatory frameworks for stablecoins and privacy tools."],
      keyRisks: ["Outright bans or severe restrictions on privacy-enhancing crypto technologies by major jurisdictions.", "Major, systemic security breach impacting a large segment of the DeFi ecosystem.", "Failure of social media platforms to effectively combat crypto-related fraud, leading to sustained reputational damage.", "Unfavorable court rulings in ongoing crypto-related legal battles."],
