      bearCase: "Persistent high Treasury yields, driven by stubborn inflation or hawkish central bank rhetoric, could continue to drain liquidity from risk assets, keeping Bitcoin under pressure. A recurrence of large-scale hacks or a failure to recover stolen funds would severely damage market trust. Furthermore, aggressive regulatory actions by bodies like the CFTC, if perceived as overly restrictive, could stifle innovation and drive crypto activity offshore, negatively impacting market growth.",
