      bearCase: "For Binance and other global exchanges, this creates significant regulatory hurdles and uncertainty, potentially forcing them to alter business models or exit key European markets. An overly protectionist stance could stifle innovation, drive crypto activity offshore, and make the EU less competitive in the global digital asset landscape.",
      neutralCase: "The incident represents a natural evolution of regulatory oversight catching up with technological advancements. It signifies a necessary clarification of roles between central banks and private crypto entities, ultimately leading to a more structured, albeit potentially slower, integration of digital assets into mainstream finance under national monetary control.",
